# DataGrid

**Language:** Write all grid-related code, comments, and commit messages in **English**.

List screens use **`DataGrid`**, **`TreeDataGrid`**, or **`DataGridWithTotals`** — not hand-rolled `v-data-table` for standard searchable lists.

## Components

| Component            | When to use                                                   |
| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `DataGrid`           | Flat searchable lists (templates, field sets, communications) |
| `TreeDataGrid`       | Parent/child rows (customer → enquiries)                      |
| `DataGridWithTotals` | Lists with footer totals                                      |

Location: `ui/src/components/DataGrid/`, `TreeDataGrid/`, `DataGridWithTotals/`.

## Frontend wiring (required props)

```vue
<DataGrid
  :api-metadata-url="UiApiGridUrlPathEnum.GRID_FIELD_SET"
  :api-data-url="UiApiUrlPathEnum.FIELD_SET_SEARCH"
  headers-auto-parser-mapping
  :fixed-conditions="fixedCondition"
  :table-label="t('item.itemList', { name: t('fieldSet') })"
/>
```

- **Metadata URL:** **`UiApiGridUrlPathEnum`** from `ui/src/enums/api.enum.ts` — GET `/uiapi/grids/...`
- **Data URL:** **`UiApiUrlPathEnum`** — usually `POST .../search` on the domain endpoint
- Do not hardcode `uiapi/grids/...` strings — use enums (legacy views may have hardcoded paths; do not copy that pattern)
- **`fixedConditions`** — scope grid to dealership, enquiry, etc. (`FixedConditionInterface[]`)
- **`defaultQueue`** — selects initial filter set when metadata defines queues (e.g. `'Customer'`)
- **`headers-auto-parser-mapping`** — common on list screens; match neighbours
- Row/header actions: **`actions`**, **`buttonActions`** — use `uuidv4()` for `key` like existing lists
- Custom column rendering: named slots `#item.{columnValue}` or `#childStatusBadge` on `TreeDataGrid`

Reference views: `CustomerList.vue`, `FieldSetManagmentList.vue`, `CommunicationsList.vue`.

## Backend — grid metadata

```
src/domain/grid/
  metadata/{domain}.metadata.ts   # columns, filterSets, subFilterSets
  enums/metadata.grid.enum.ts     # GridMetadata enum
  grid.service.ts                 # dispatches metadata + search
src/ui-api/grids/grids.controller.ts   # GET /uiapi/grids/{name}
```

Adding a new grid:

1. Create **`XxxMetadata`** class extending **`BaseMetadata`** in `metadata/`
2. Register in **`GridService`** constructor and add getter method
3. Add **`@Get('/grids/...')`** in **`grids.controller.ts`**
4. Add **`UiApiGridUrlPathEnum`** entry in `api.enum.ts`
5. Ensure domain **`POST .../search`** exists (`UiApiUrlPathEnum`) — often already on domain controller

Metadata columns use `text`, `value`, `sortable`, `sortData`, optional `parse` / `html` from grid enums.

## Search flow

```
View (DataGrid)
  → GET apiMetadataUrl  → GridService → XxxMetadata.grid()
  → POST apiDataUrl     → DomainService.search(FilterParams)
```

`FilterParams` from `@domain/grid/interfaces` — grid builds payload from metadata filter sets.

## i18n

- Table titles and action labels via **`t()`** — see `i18n.mdc`
- Column headers come from metadata `text` (backend) — user-facing column labels are defined in metadata classes

## Before finishing

- [ ] `UiApiGridUrlPathEnum` + `UiApiUrlPathEnum` — no hardcoded grid URLs
- [ ] Metadata class registered in `GridService` + `grids.controller.ts`
- [ ] `fixedConditions` scoped correctly for the screen
- [ ] Custom cells use slots — not template hacks that bypass grid parsers
- [ ] Match neighbouring list view props (`show-filter-sets`, `hide-footer`, `auto-height`, …)
